{"id": "EUVD-2026-86802", "enisaUuid": "92dabd8c-56b6-3b64-ab5c-7bfba5116737", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\npowerpc/eeh: Fix recursive locking on devices without EEH sensitive driver\n\nThe commit 1010b4c012b0 (\"powerpc/eeh: Make EEH driver device hotplug\nsafe\") refactored the EEH code such that the pci_rescan_remove_lock is\nheld at the beginning of eeh_handle_normal_event() and the\neeh_reset_device() is called with that lock being held. Looks like the\ncommit missed to remove the existing lock/unlock inside eeh_rmv_device()\nwhich is no longer necessary. This is causing the eehd to hang on the\nlock which it actually holds when that code path is taken.\n\n[<0>] 0xc00000011c78f870\n[<0>] __switch_to+0xfc/0x1a0\n[<0>] pci_lock_rescan_remove+0x30/0x44\n[<0>] eeh_rmv_device+0x290/0x2e0\n[<0>] eeh_pe_dev_traverse+0x80/0x130\n[<0>] eeh_reset_device+0xcc/0x23c\n[<0>] eeh_handle_normal_event+0x830/0xa80\n[<0>] eeh_event_handler+0xf8/0x190\n[<0>] kthread+0x194/0x1b0\n[<0>] start_kernel_thread+0x14/0x18\n\nThe issue is seen for cases where the errors are detected on the PHB\ndirectly AND|OR for devices where the driver error_detected() returns\nPCI_ERS_RESULT_NEED_RESET, and driver being not EEH sensitive(i.e no\nerror handlers like slot_reset(), resume() etc defined).", "datePublished": "2026-09-25T10:22:57", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:11:14", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3833dfae0680b6b16e2469fbc90aa48376311cd8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24524fca27da674668941440e8e05cdfec0b0222", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a58531181363219fa5de2b53d5d7274dcdfca98b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/460fab22b65138531082910702f74b048b25237b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/102e3dc5ab5ba052e294819e83384166b242c1ec", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/2920af33d097ca335e492b346af70b72986ad6dc", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/85d8eaefc052cf3e5ae2c7bafeda2db68b8898b4", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/c5e68706527968282e49de205cc2b935823cb88a"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-97948", "GHSA-wgj5-j7wg-2jm2"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0f7c1307-ceab-3474-8985-421814578a35", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.6.102 <6.6.158"}, {"id": "110dbc5b-325f-3a2a-b218-ef4516a10f1b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.1.148 <6.1.189"}, {"id": "11b0047e-0f34-328b-a4cf-c98a583cb98b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1010b4c012b0d78dfb9d3132b49aa2ef024a07a7 <c5e68706527968282e49de205cc2b935823cb88a"}, {"id": "17d63f39-6ae0-30cd-8115-e7b3835b0292", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.12.42 <6.12.111"}, {"id": "1c1105b4-35f4-347b-81aa-78e54d3bea57", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "19d5036e7ad766cf212aebec23b9f1d7924a62bc"}, {"id": "1e80405b-d710-3276-8ef7-340f35e5f69f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1010b4c012b0d78dfb9d3132b49aa2ef024a07a7 <85d8eaefc052cf3e5ae2c7bafeda2db68b8898b4"}, {"id": "3e4333e1-d2ab-30a0-9b6a-3fa74e3472b5", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "487cc624-712e-3071-bbf8-2ac9c9255c3b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "5.10.241 <5.10.271"}, {"id": "52160012-36a6-3cc6-bdeb-f637b4a65e96", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "1010b4c012b0d78dfb9d3132b49aa2ef024a07a7 <2920af33d097ca335e492b346af70b72986ad6dc"}, {"id": "71b87f19-b070-304b-9d5d-d08b5a76cba6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "a426e8a6ae161f51888585b065db0f8f93ab2e16 <460fab22b65138531082910702f74b048b25237b"}, {"id": "744ff20f-ba88-38f6-89ab-ddfe7b65fa37", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor